 ### [Order Independent Transparency Approaches](3611-order-independent-transparency-approaches.md)
-This family encompasses methods for rendering transparent point-based models without relying on strict depth sorting. It addresses the non-commutative nature of translucent compositing by approximating the correct order of operations or using alternative accumulation strategies [G]. It is chosen when scenes have a limited number of transparent layers and GPU memory is constrained, though it may introduce approximation artifacts if the layer limit is exceeded [G].
